  replayed 60 cell(s); gate: ABORT: the true series does not outscore the decoy control in every round (threat-model margin 1:+0.0004 2:-0.0001 3:-0.0006; mean -0.0001) - round(s) 2, 3 carry no series-specific information, so a ranking would be meaningless there.  The decoy is another real client, so beating it requires the series to drive the update more than the unobservable pre-round state does; round 1 is the classic case, where that state dominates the local delta.  DIAGNOSIS: the signal itself exists - with the pre-round state known (oracle arm) the true series beats the decoy by +0.0118 (mean), 1:+0.0004 2:+0.0237 3:+0.0114 per round - but at this knowledge level the unmodelled state gap buries it (-0.9% of the ceiling survives).  So a ranking stage needs a stronger knowledge model, not a better candidate list.

