------------------------------------------------------------------------
FEASIBILITY GATE (may the ranking stage run?)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRECONDITION: the run must be reproducible.  Two model builds
under the build seed must give identical initial weights, else
every number below - and the verdict - is one unreproducible
sample and no ranking stage may be built on it.
THREE INDEPENDENT conditions: (1) the oracle replay must
reproduce the update exactly for a noise-free arm (every cell
bit-identical, or at worst to float rounding), or with a
residual equal to the injected noise for a noise-injecting one -
else the pipeline model is wrong; (2) the
true deltas must be separable, else no ranking could work; (3)
the true series must outscore the decoy control in EVERY
evaluated round - a mean alone can be decided by the last
decimal, and a round that the decoy reproduces just as well
carries no series-specific information at all.

precondition: build determinism OK (initial weights digest e9b036e556c916fa)

config                 oracle exact  oracle cos   B cos      decoy cos   margin    separation 
none                   100%          1.000000     0.912685   0.912790    -0.0001   0.1578     
clip_only_c2           ~exact        1.000000     0.911918   0.912078    -0.0002   0.1619     
gaussian_c2_s0.001     n/a (noise)   0.997482     0.909403   0.909520    -0.0001   0.1606     
gaussian_c2_s0.01      n/a (noise)   0.815014     0.744264   0.744407    -0.0001   0.1089     

condition 1 (did the oracle replay reproduce the update?) is
mechanism-aware: a noise-free arm must reproduce the update
exactly (at worst to float rounding), while a
noise-injecting arm CANNOT be - the draw is not observable and
not reproducible even with the whole pre-round state - so there
the residual must instead equal the injected noise, i.e.
residual/||noise|| = 1.00 (tolerance 0.10):
  none                   bit-exact (100% of cells bit-identical, mean rel_L2 0.00e+00)
  clip_only_c2           exact to float rounding (0% of cells bit-identical, mean rel_L2 1.16e-07)
  gaussian_c2_s0.001     noise-explained: residual/noise = 1.0000 (||noise|| 0.142156)
  gaussian_c2_s0.01      noise-explained: residual/noise = 1.0000 (||noise|| 1.421173)

per-round decoy margin (realistic arm: true minus decoy cosine) - a
round with a negative margin carries no series information:
  none                   round 1: +0.0004   round 2: -0.0001   round 3: -0.0006
  clip_only_c2           round 1: +0.0004   round 2: -0.0001   round 3: -0.0008
  gaussian_c2_s0.001     round 1: +0.0004   round 2: -0.0001   round 3: -0.0007
  gaussian_c2_s0.01      round 1: +0.0004   round 2: -0.0002   round 3: -0.0006

signal ceiling - the SAME comparison with the pre-round state
known (oracle arm), i.e. how much series information the update
carries at all.  A large ceiling next to a ~0 threat-model
margin means the information exists but the unmodelled
pre-round state buries it, so the obstacle is the knowledge
model, not the candidate list:
  none                   round 1: +0.0004   round 2: +0.0237   round 3: +0.0114   (threat model keeps -0.9% of it)
  clip_only_c2           round 1: +0.0004   round 2: +0.0235   round 3: +0.0109   (threat model keeps -1.4% of it)
  gaussian_c2_s0.001     round 1: +0.0004   round 2: +0.0234   round 3: +0.0109   (threat model keeps -1.0% of it)
  gaussian_c2_s0.01      round 1: +0.0004   round 2: +0.0202   round 3: +0.0089   (threat model keeps -1.5% of it)

  none                   ABORT: the true series does not outscore the decoy control in every round (threat-model margin 1:+0.0004 2:-0.0001 3:-0.0006; mean -0.0001) - round(s) 2, 3 carry no series-specific information, so a ranking would be meaningless there.  The decoy is another real client, so beating it requires the series to drive the update more than the unobservable pre-round state does; round 1 is the classic case, where that state dominates the local delta.  DIAGNOSIS: the signal itself exists - with the pre-round state known (oracle arm) the true series beats the decoy by +0.0118 (mean), 1:+0.0004 2:+0.0237 3:+0.0114 per round - but at this knowledge level the unmodelled state gap buries it (-0.9% of the ceiling survives).  So a ranking stage needs a stronger knowledge model, not a better candidate list.
  clip_only_c2           ABORT: the true series does not outscore the decoy control in every round (threat-model margin 1:+0.0004 2:-0.0001 3:-0.0008; mean -0.0002) - round(s) 2, 3 carry no series-specific information, so a ranking would be meaningless there.  The decoy is another real client, so beating it requires the series to drive the update more than the unobservable pre-round state does; round 1 is the classic case, where that state dominates the local delta.  DIAGNOSIS: the signal itself exists - with the pre-round state known (oracle arm) the true series beats the decoy by +0.0116 (mean), 1:+0.0004 2:+0.0235 3:+0.0109 per round - but at this knowledge level the unmodelled state gap buries it (-1.4% of the ceiling survives).  So a ranking stage needs a stronger knowledge model, not a better candidate list.
